30
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:18,820
A migration triggered by the chairman of the Triborough

31
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:22,060
Bridge and Tunnel Authority, the politically powerful

32
00:02:22,061 --> 00:02:26,860
Robert Moses, builder of the 1964 World's Fair, Lincoln

33
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:30,860
Center, and Shea Stadium.

34
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:33,440
To create room for the Verrazano's substantial

35
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:37,080
approach roads, Moses ousted 8,000 Brooklyn

36
00:02:37,180 --> 00:02:39,240
inhabitants from their homes.

37
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:43,640
In the 1930s, 40s, 50s, as roads were being built in New

38
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:46,820
York, and we were building it before there was federal aid

39
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:50,360
for roads, Bob Moses had the power of eminent domain

40
00:02:50,361 --> 00:02:52,700
as the city's construction coordinator.

41
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,740
He can decide that it was in the public interest

42
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:57,740
to take your house, to take your property.

43
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:00,400
And there's very little that you could do other than go

44
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:02,280
through the political process.

45
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:04,740
He would have design drawings and engineers come out,

46
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:07,740
and then you would have to move.

47
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,840
Nobody would think of ever bucking City Hall or Robert

48
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:11,740
Moses.

49
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:14,620
Nor did anyone buck Moses when he nixed

50
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:18,580
rapid transit, forcing everyone to travel the Verrazano

51
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,020
