52
00:03:20,021 --> 00:03:22,120
You needed a car, which said you were from some kind

53
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:23,760
of an economic class.

54
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:27,000
So in many ways, it polarized the city.

55
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:30,200
And so designing a bridge the wrong way

56
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:33,100
to not introduce transit created one community that was more

57
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:34,640
affluent and more white.

58
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:36,440
And that was the community of Staten Island.

59
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:41,080
And it left Brooklyn to be more minority, a poorer community.

60
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:43,940
As he'd done before with his bridges,

61
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:47,420
Robert Moses hired the now elderly master bridge builder,

62
00:03:47,421 --> 00:03:48,880
Othmar Amon.

63
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:52,160
Critics charged that Amon may have designed the bridge,

64
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:56,200
but he designed Robert Moses Bridge.

65
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:58,400
Cost spiraled quickly.

66
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:04,140
At completion, the Verrazano cost over $320 million.

67
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:09,240
Workers spent a year building the Verrazano's two towers.

68
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:11,640
Built perpendicular to the Earth's surface,

69
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:15,180
they are 1 and 5 eighths inches farther apart at their tops

70
00:04:15,181 --> 00:04:17,820
than at their bases due to the curvature of the Earth.

71
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:24,320
The 690-foot-tall towers are higher than most

72
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:28,120
